# Filter Hz 1.3.0: performance edit keeps stock's signed depth on the FX track's DELAY page
# (a depth is not a frequency). PERF mode, FUNC + BD opens macro 1's edit, BD held, HPF and
# LPF turned (HPF 32, LPF 96 set first, so the graph does not depend on the case before). The reference was checked against the same case on a link image without
# the module, which shows the same signed depth.
# Clears macro 1 (edit list: <CLEAR>, YES) before and after, so it leaves macro 1 empty. PERF is
# tapped three times: mode on, edit off, mode off (edit itself opens with FUNC + BD).
name: filter-hz-perf-edit
state: changes
# FX is a toggle (pressed on the FX track it goes back to the drum track), so BD is selected first.
hold TRK
key BD
release TRK
key FX
key SRC
wait 3500
cc 20 32
cc 21 96
wait 300
key PERF
wait 300
hold FUNC
key BD
release FUNC
wait 500
key LEFT x3
key RIGHT x2
wait 300
key YES
wait 500
screen cleared
hold BD
nudge E +1
nudge E +6
nudge F +1
nudge F -4
wait 750
screen perf
expect perf == ref region 0 40 128 24
release BD
wait 300
key LEFT x3
key RIGHT x2
wait 300
key YES
wait 500
key PERF
wait 300
key PERF
